  "body": "In the [resource selection algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-media-load-algorithm)'s *children* mode, after the *Waiting* step, when a new `source` element is inserted:\n\n> ⌛ Set the element's [delaying-the-load-event flag](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#delaying-the-load-event-flag) back to true (this [delays the load event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#delay-the-load-event) again, in case it hasn't been fired yet).\n\nThis doesn't check the [lazy loading attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#lazy-loading-attribute), unlike the step at the start of the algorithm (after #12970). The algorithm then jumps back to *find next candidate* and reaches the [resource fetch algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-media-load-resource), which parks:\n\n> If the [will lazy load element steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#will-lazy-load-element-steps) given the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#media-element) return true: … Return.\n\n...without clearing the flag. So for a below-viewport `<video loading=lazy><source type=video/unsupported></video>`, inserting a `<source src=...>` while the document is still loading delays the document's `load` event until the video intersects the viewport, which may be never.\n\nMaybe the step should have the same Eager/scripting-disabled condition, or the lazy branch of the resource fetch algorithm should set the flag to false.\n\n(Found while fixing #12854.)\n",
